  "goodToKnow": "Das Kabarett in German-speaking countries is mainly political and social satire on stage, different from the glamorous cabaret of Liza Minnelli's film. It flourished in Weimar Berlin, was suppressed by the Nazis, and revived after the war with ensembles like the Münchner Lach- und Schießgesellschaft. Der Kabarettist (die Kabarettistin) performs it; TV shows like Die Anstalt keep the tradition. Plural: die Kabaretts."
